This is like my rambling. But I want to know your opinion.

I wondered which is fast `base?.at(-1)` and `base?.[base.length - 1`. I've tried to bench with `mitata` but the almost same, I think it's hard to compare the execution time is too short. But I benchmarked within my Chrome console with this code:

```js
const base = "abcdef";
const iterations = 1_000_000;

console.time("at method");
for (let i = 0; i < iterations; i++) {
  const char = base?.at(-1);
}
console.timeEnd("at method");

console.time("index method");
for (let i = 0; i < iterations; i++) {
  const char = base?.[base.length - 1];
}
console.timeEnd("index method");
