I think this implementation will compile the regex object for each `parseAcceptValue` calling.
So I prefer to declare the regex in the root scope.

```suggestion
const parseAcceptValueRegex = /;(?=(?:(?:[^"]*"){2})*[^"]*$)/
const parseAcceptValue = ({ value, index }: { value: string; index: number }) => {
  const parts = value
    .trim()
    .split(parseAcceptValueRegex)
    .map((s) => s.trim())
  const type = parts[0]
  if (!type) {
    return null
  }

  const params = parseParams(parts.slice(1))
  const q = parseQuality(params.q)

  return { type, params, q, index }
}
```

